      "id": 1,
      "text": "Snowflake was founded in 1878 by Mormon pioneers Erastus Snow and William Jordan Flake.",
      "sourceSentenceIds": [
        3
      ],
      "sourceLabels": [
        "Wikipedia"
      ],
      "source": "https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Snowflake%2C_Arizona",
      "category": "history",
      "quality": "good"
    },
    {
      "id": 2,
      "text": "The town’s historic district includes 26 homes listed on the National Register of Historic Places.",
      "sourceSentenceIds": [
        7
      ],
      "sourceLabels": [
        "Web source 2"
      ],
      "source": "https://www.explore.com/1867139/old-west-arizona-snowflake-town-outdoor-activities-colorful-charming-downtown/",
      "category": "landmark",
      "quality": "good"
    },
    {
      "id": 3,
      "text": "Snowflake’s Old West heritage is celebrated at the Snowflake Heritage Foundation, the Stinson Museum, and the Latter‑Day Saints Temple.",
      "sourceSentenceIds": [
        1
      ],
      "sourceLabels": [
        "Web source 2"
      ],
      "source": "https://www.explore.com/1867139/old-west-arizona-snowflake-town-outdoor-activities-colorful-charming-downtown/",
      "category": "culture",
      "quality": "good"
    },
    {
      "id": 4,
      "text": "Just a short drive away, Meteor Crater preserves one of Earth’s best‑preserved impact sites, formed about 50,000 years ago.",
      "sourceSentenceIds": [
        8
      ],
      "sourceLabels": [
        "Web source 2"
      ],
      "source": "https://www.explore.com/1867139/old-west-arizona-snowflake-town-outdoor-activities-colorful-charming-downtown/",
      "category": "nature",
      "quality": "good"
    },
    {
      "id": 5,
      "text": "The town nestles in Silver Creek Valley, part of Arizona’s White Mountains, giving it a distinctive high‑elevation setting.",
      "sourceSentenceIds": [
        2
      ],
      "sourceLabels": [
        "Web source 2"
      ],
      "source": "https://www.explore.com/1867139/old-west-arizona-snowflake-town-outdoor-activities-colorful-charming-downtown/",
      "category": "nature",
      "quality": "good"
    },
    {
      "id": 6,
      "text": "Snowflake’s name honors its founder, Erastus Snow, a prominent Mormon leader who helped establish the town in the late 19th century.",
